COMPARE_H2 = 'Business loan leads compared with other ways to win clients'
COMPARE = [
    'Most brokerages grow through a mix of referrals, introducer relationships, their own marketing and bought-in leads. Each has its place. Referrals from accountants and existing clients are valuable but hard to scale, and introducer relationships take years to build. Running your own paid search and social campaigns can work well, but it needs budget, expertise and constant attention, and you pay for every click whether or not it turns into an enquiry.',
    'Buying leads sits in between. Someone else carries the cost and risk of the advertising, the landing pages and the qualification, and you only buy enquiries that match the criteria you choose. That makes your cost of acquisition predictable, and it lets you scale up or down without hiring a marketing team or committing to a long-term advertising budget.',
    'The catch with many lead sources is quality. Shared leads, aged data and vague enquiries quickly erode any saving. That is why Loanleaf focuses on exclusivity, qualification and context: each lead goes to one partner, it has passed our filters, and it comes with the full set of answers and a record of consent. The aim is simple: fewer leads you can’t help, and more conversations that turn into deals.',
    'Buying leads works best alongside your existing channels, not instead of them. Many partners use Loanleaf to keep their pipeline steady between referral peaks, to test a new finance type or loan size before investing in their own marketing, or to give new team members a consistent flow of enquiries to work.',
]

